  "artifact": "PX4_FEASIBILITY",
  "mag": "NOT RUN. PX4Adapter reads the magnetometer from HIGHRES_IMU and gates it on the `fields_updated` bitmask (csia/aircraft/adapters/px4.py:107-123, FIELD_XMAG). ArduPilotAdapter reads it from SCALED_IMU with no such bitmask (ardupilot.py:141-148). Driving the ArduPilot word alphabet through the PX4 branch would compare two different interfaces and report the difference as a semantic one. Item 24 says not to force identical semantics.",
  "px4_specific_state_not_present_on_ardupilot": {
    "estimator_status_ratios": "PX4 reports innovation RATIOS where ArduPilot reports variances; the adapter tags the source rather than conflating them (px4.py:196-200). Neither reaches the frozen core.",
    "fields_updated_bitmask": "HIGHRES_IMU carries a per-field validity bitmask. This is a genuine extra source state -- 'this message arrived but this field was not updated' -- and PX4Adapter reads it (px4.py:107). ArduPilot's SCALED_IMU has no equivalent."
  },
